{"timestamp":"2026-05-11T22:06:28.475Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"Yes. `.git/entire/preferences.json` would still be local.\n\nMore specifically:\n\n- It is local to one Git clone.\n- It is not committed.\n- It is not pushed.\n- It is shared by linked worktrees that belong to the same clone, because they share the Git common dir.\n- It does not follow you to another clone of the same repo.\n- It does not apply to other repos.\n\nSo it sits between the other two options:\n\n```text\n.entire/settings.local.json       local to one worktree\n.git/entire/preferences.json      local to one clone, shared by that clone's worktrees\n~/.config/entire/preferences.json local to one user machine, across repos\n```\n\nIf the core requirement is “local, not committed, but do not reconfigure every worktree,” `.git/entire/preferences.json` is the only one of these three that matches.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
