{"timestamp":"2026-05-11T22:24:25.574Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"**Design Section 2: Save Paths And Merge Logic**\n\nWe’ll add a clone-local preferences file resolved from Git’s common dir:\n\n```text\n<git-common-dir>/entire/preferences.json\n```\n\nIt is not committed, not pushed, and is shared by linked worktrees in the same clone. The file should be general-purpose, but only these fields are in scope now:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"review\": {\n    \"claude-code\": {\n      \"skills\": [\"...\"],\n      \"prompt\": \"...\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"review_fix_agent\": \"claude-code\"\n}\n```\n\n`entire review --edit` will save picker changes there instead of `.entire/settings.json`. To avoid polluting preferences with unrelated project settings, the picker should load and save the preferences file directly, not load merged settings and write that back.\n\n`settings.Load()` should merge in preferences after project settings and before/with local overrides. The important implementation detail is that `review` must get a real merge handler in `mergeJSON`, because today local `review` is decoded for validation but dropped. For `review`, the preference/local map should wholesale replace the base map. `review_fix_agent` can keep the existing non-empty string behavior.\n\nPrecedence should be:\n\n```text\n.entire/settings.json\n<git-common-dir>/entire/preferences.json\n.entire/settings.local.json\n```\n\nThat keeps existing committed defaults usable, lets clone-local review preferences override them, and preserves the strongest local override layer if someone already uses `settings.local.json`.\n\nDoes this section look right before I continue to the migration and nudge UX?","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
