{"timestamp":"2026-05-11T22:51:09.991Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","status":"completed","call_id":"call_hdVLJut6ByUK6WbTZdSOA0QZ","name":"apply_patch","input":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-11-review-config-local-design.md\n+# Review Config Clone-Local Preferences Design\n+\n+## Goal\n+\n+`entire review --edit` must stop writing personal review preferences to the\n+project-committed `.entire/settings.json`. Review skill selections, per-agent\n+review prompts, and the selected review-fix agent should be stored locally.\n+\n+The local storage must also avoid forcing users to reconfigure review in every\n+linked worktree of the same clone.\n+\n+## Storage\n+\n+Add a clone-local preferences file at:\n+\n+```text\n+<git-common-dir>/entire/preferences.json\n+```\n+\n+The path must be resolved through Git's common dir, not by assuming the current\n+worktree has a `.git/` directory. This keeps the file shared by linked\n+worktrees in the same clone while remaining uncommitted and unpushed.\n+\n+The file is a general preferences file, but this change only uses review fields:\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"review\": {\n+    \"claude-code\": {\n+      \"skills\": [\"...\"],\n+      \"prompt\": \"...\"\n+    }\n+  },\n+  \"review_fix_agent\": \"claude-code\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Save Behavior\n+\n+The review picker save paths should write to clone-local preferences instead of\n+`.entire/settings.json`:\n+\n+- `SaveReviewConfig`\n+- `SaveReviewFixAgent`\n+- combined review config and fix-agent save\n+\n+Picker save code should load and save the preferences file directly. It should\n+not load fully merged settings and write them back, because that would copy\n+unrelated project settings into the preferences file.\n+\n+## Load And Merge Behavior\n+\n+Settings should load in this precedence order:\n+\n+```text\n+.entire/settings.json\n+<git-common-dir>/entire/preferences.json\n+.entire/settings.local.json\n+```\n+\n+This preserves committed project defaults, lets clone-local review preferences\n+override those defaults, and keeps `.entire/settings.local.json` as the final\n+worktree-local override layer.\n+\n+`mergeJSON` needs an explicit `review` merge handler. Today it decodes `review`\n+for validation but does not copy it into the merged result. The new behavior\n+should wholesale replace the base `review` map when an override file provides\n+one. `review_fix_agent` can continue using the existing non-empty string merge\n+behavior.\n+\n+## Migration And Prompting\n+\n+Migration should happen only when `.entire/settings.json` contains `review` or\n+`review_fix_agent`.\n+\n+When project-level review settings exist, `entire review` should ask the user to\n+migrate them to local preferences. The prompt should continue appearing until\n+the project-level review keys are removed.\n+\n+On migration:\n+\n+1. Load existing clone-local preferences.\n+2. Move project-level `review` and `review_fix_agent` into\n+   `<git-common-dir>/entire/preferences.json`.\n+3. Save the preferences file.\n+4. Remove only `review` and `review_fix_agent` from `.entire/settings.json`.\n+\n+Writing preferences first avoids data loss if the command exits midway. If both\n+project and preference copies temporarily exist, preferences win during settings\n+load, and the migration prompt appears again until the project file is cleaned.\n+\n+If `.entire/settings.json` has no review fields, `entire review` should not\n+prompt.\n+\n+Picker saves should always write future review changes to clone-local\n+preferences, regardless of whether migration was accepted.\n+\n+For non-interactive runs, migration prompting should degrade to a warning rather\n+than blocking.\n+\n+## Out Of Scope\n+\n+- User-global review preferences under `~/.config/entire`.\n+- Writing Entire-owned keys to Git config.\n+- E2E tests with real agents.\n+- Broad preference fields unrelated to review.\n+\n+## Test Plan\n+\n+Keep tests focused:\n+\n+- Retarget existing picker save tests so they assert writes to clone-local\n+  preferences instead of `.entire/settings.json`.\n+- Add a settings merge test proving `review` from an override source is not\n+  dropped and wholesale replaces the project-level `review` map.\n+- Add migration coverage proving project-level review settings move to\n+  preferences and are removed from project settings.\n+- Add no-op coverage proving migration prompting is not triggered when project\n+  settings have no review fields.\n+\n+Verification should use unit tests first. Do not run real-agent E2E tests unless\n+explicitly requested.\n*** End Patch\n"}}
