l preferences.\n  - Update user-facing copy that still says settings are saved to `.entire/settings.json`.\n- Add `cmd/entire/cli/review/migration.go`\n  - Detect project-level review keys by reading `.entire/settings.json` directly.\n  - Prompt when those keys exist.\n  - Migrate values to clone-local preferences first, then remove the keys from project settings.\n- Modify `cmd/entire/cli/review/cmd.go`\n  - Invoke migration prompting after mode validation and before review/edit/fix/findings handling.\n  - Reuse `Deps.PromptYN` when provided; fall back to the existing real y/N prompt path.\n- Modify `cmd/entire/cli/review/export_test.go`\n  - Expose only the migration helper inputs needed by external tests, if direct command tests are too awkward.\n- Modify tests:\n  - `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings_test.go`\n  - `cmd/entire/cli/review/picker_test.go`\n  - `cmd/entire/cli/review/cmd_test.go` or new `cmd/entire/cli/review/migration_test.go`\n\nDo not commit this plan or spec unless explicitly asked.\n\n---\n\n### Task 1: Add Clone-Local Review Preferences In Settings\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing merge tests**\n\nAdd tests in `settings_test.go`:\n\n```go\nfunc TestMergeJSON_ReviewWholesaleReplacesBase(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\ts := &EntireSettings{Review: map[string]ReviewConfig{\n\t\t\"claude-code\": {Skills: []string{\"/old\"}},\n\t}}\n\traw := []byte(`{\"review\":{\"codex\":{\"prompt\":\"new\"}}}`)\n\n\tif err := mergeJSON(s, raw); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"mergeJSON: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tif _, ok := s.Review[\"claude-code\"]; ok {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"base review entry survived wholesale replace: %+v\", s.Review)\n\t}\n\tif got := s.Review[\"codex\"].Prompt; got != \"new\" {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"codex prompt = %q, want new\", got)\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nAdd a load-precedence test using `testutil.InitRepo`, `t.Chdir`, and no `t.Parallel`:\n\n```go\nfunc TestLoad_AppliesClonePreferencesBeforeLocalSettings(t *testing.T) {\n\ttmp := t.TempDir()\n\ttestutil.InitRepo(t, tmp)\n\tt.Chdir(tmp)\n\tsession.ClearGitCommonDirCache()\n\n\t// .entire/settings.json has project default review.\n\t// .git/entire/preferences.json has clone-local review.\n\t// .entire/settings.local.json has final worktree-local review.\n\t// Assert settings.Load returns the local review, proving precedence.\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run settings tests and verify failure**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings -run 'TestMergeJSON_ReviewWholesaleReplacesBase|TestLoad_AppliesClonePreferencesBeforeLocalSettings' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: fail because `mergeJSON` currently drops `review`, and `Load` does not read clone-local preferences.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Implement narrow preferences support**\n\nIn `settings.go`, import `github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/session`.\n\nAdd a narrow struct near `EntireSettings` or after `ReviewConfig`:\n\n```go\ntype ClonePreferences struct {\n\tReview         map[string]ReviewConfig `json:\"review,omitempty\"`\n\tReviewFixAgent string                  `json:\"review_fix_agent,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n\nAdd helpers:\n\n```go\nconst ClonePreferencesFile = \"entire/preferences.json\"\n\nfunc ClonePreferencesPath(ctx context.Context) (string, error) {\n\tcommonDir, err := session.GetGitCommonDir(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", err\n\t}\n\treturn filepath.Join(commonDir, ClonePreferencesFile), nil\n}\n\nfunc LoadClonePreferences(ctx context.Context) (*ClonePreferences, error) {\n\tpath, err := ClonePreferencesPath(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, err\n\t}\n\treturn loadClonePreferencesFromFile(path)\n}\n\nfunc SaveClonePreferences(ctx context.Context, prefs *ClonePreferences) error {\n\tpath, err := ClonePreferencesPath(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\treturn saveClonePreferencesToFile(prefs, path)\n}\n```\n\nImplement `loadClonePreferencesFromFile` with `json.Decoder.DisallowUnknownFields`, returning an empty `ClonePreferences` for missing files. Implement `saveClonePreferencesToFile` with `os.MkdirAll(filepath.Dir(path), 0o750)` and `jsonutil.MarshalIndentWithNewline`, writing `0o644`.\n\nDo not use `saveToFile` for preferences, because `EntireSettings.Enabled` lacks `omitempty` and would write unrelated `\"enabled\": true`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Apply preferences in `Load`**\n\nChange `Load` to resolve three layers:\n\n```text\nproject settings path\nclone preferences path, if the current directory is in a git repo\nsettings.local path\n```\n\nChange `loadMergedSettings` to accept an optional preferences path:\n\n```go\nfunc loadMergedSettings(settingsFileAbs, preferencesFileAbs, localSettingsFileAbs string) (*EntireSettings, error)\n```\n\nIf resolving the git common dir fails, skip clone preferences so settings can still load outside a repo. If the preferences path exists but is malformed, return a load error.\n\nApply preferences with field-specific logic:\n\n```go\nfunc applyClonePreferences(s *EntireSettings, prefs *ClonePreferences) {\n\tif prefs == nil {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tif prefs.Review != nil {\n\t\ts.Review = prefs.Review\n\t}\n\tif prefs.ReviewFixAgent != \"\" {\n\t\ts.ReviewFixAgent = prefs.ReviewFixAgent\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Fix `mergeJSON` for `.entire/settings.local.json`**\n\nAdd a `review` handler after scalar/structured merges:\n\n```go\nif reviewRaw, ok := raw[\"review\"]; ok {\n\tvar review map[string]ReviewConfig\n\tif err := json.Unmarshal(reviewRaw, &review); err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"parsing review field: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tsettings.Review = review\n}\n```\n\nThis is needed for `settings.local.json` and any future JSON override using `mergeJSON`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run settings tests and verify pass**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings -run 'TestMergeJSON_ReviewWholesaleReplacesBase|TestLoad_AppliesClonePreferencesBeforeLocalSettings' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: pass.\n\n---\n\n### Task 2: Save Review Picker Choices To Clone Preferences\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/review/picker.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/review/picker_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Retarget existing picker save tests**\n\nUpdate these tests to assert clone-local preferences are written:\n\n- `TestSaveReviewConfig_PersistsSettings`\n- `TestSaveReviewConfig_PreservesReviewFixAgent`\n- `TestSaveReviewFixAgent_PersistsSettings`\n- `TestSaveReviewConfig_ReturnsErrorOnMalformedSettings`\n\nUse `settings.LoadClonePreferences(context.Background())` for direct persistence assertions, and `settings.Load(context.Background())` when asserting effective merged settings.\n\nFor the malformed-file test, make the malformed file `<git-common-dir>/entire/preferences.json`, not `.entire/settings.json`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run picker save tests and verify failure**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/review -run 'TestSaveReviewConfig|TestSaveReviewFixAgent' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: fail because save helpers still write project settings.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Update save helpers**\n\nIn `picker.go`, change:\n\n```go\nsettings.Load(ctx)\nsettings.Save(ctx, s)\n```\n\nto preferences-specific load/save:\n\n```go\nprefs, err := settings.LoadClonePreferences(ctx)\nif err != nil {\n\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"load review preferences before save: %w\", err)\n}\nif prefs == nil {\n\tprefs = &settings.ClonePreferences{}\n}\nprefs.Review = review\nif err := settings.SaveClonePreferences(ctx, prefs); err != nil {\n\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"save review preferences: %w\", err)\n}\n```\n\nDo the analogous update for `ReviewFixAgent` and the combined save.\n\nPreserve existing behavior that `SaveReviewConfig` does not wipe `ReviewFixAgent`, and `SaveReviewFixAgent` does not wipe `Review`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Update user-facing picker copy**\n\nChange strings in `ConfirmFirstRunSetup` and `RunReviewConfigPicker` that say `.entire/settings.json` to refer to local review preferences. Avoid exposing the hidden path as the main UX text.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nThey're saved as local review preferences; edit later with `entire review --edit`.\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Run picker save tests and verify pass**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/review -run 'TestSaveReviewConfig|TestSaveReviewFixAgent' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: pass.\n\n---\n\n### Task 3: Add Project Settings Migration Prompt\n\n**Files:**\n- Add: `cmd/entire/cli/review/migration.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/review/cmd.go`\n- Modify if needed: `cmd/entire/cli/review/export_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/review/migration_test.go` or `cmd/entire/cli/review/cmd_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing migration tests**\n\nAdd focused tests with temp git repos. Do not use `t.Parallel` because tests use `t.Chdir`.\n\nTest accepted migration:\n\n```go\nfunc TestReviewSettingsMigration_MovesProjectReviewToClonePreferences(t *testing.T) {\n\ttmp := t.TempDir()\n\ttestutil.InitRepo(t, tmp)\n\tt.Chdir(tmp)\n\tsession.ClearGitCommonDirCache()\n\n\t// Write .entire/settings.json with enabled/log_level plus review and review_fix_agent.\n\t// Invoke the migration helper with a prompt stub that returns true.\n\t// Assert preferences has review and review_fix_agent.\n\t// Assert .entire/settings.json still has unrelated keys but no review keys.\n}\n```\n\nTest no prompt when project has no review keys:\n\n```go\nfunc TestReviewSettingsMigration_SkipsWhenProjectHasNoReviewKeys(t *testing.T) {\n\t// Write .entire/settings.json without review fields.\n\t// Use a prompt stub that fails the test if called.\n\t// Assert no preferences file is created.\n}\n```\n\nAdd one non-interactive test if the helper takes `canPrompt` as an input:\n\n```go\nfunc TestReviewSettingsMigration_NonInteractiveWarnsAndDoesNotMigrate(t *testing.T)\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run migration tests and verify failure**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/review -run 'TestReviewSettingsMigration' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: fail because migration helpers do not exist.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Implement project review key detection**\n\nIn `migration.go`, resolve `.entire/settings.json` with `paths.AbsPath(ctx, settings.EntireSettingsFile)`.\n\nRead the file directly:\n\n```go\nraw := map[string]json.RawMessage{}\n```\n\nTreat either key as project-level review settings:\n\n```go\n_, hasReview := raw[\"review\"]\n_, hasFixAgent := raw[\"review_fix_agent\"]\n```\n\nUse key presence, not just non-empty values, so empty project-level review keys are cleaned up and the prompt self-quiets.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Implement migration**\n\nOn accepted migration:\n\n1. Load clone preferences.\n2. If project `review` exists and preferences `Review` is nil or empty, copy project review into preferences.\n3. If project `review_fix_agent` exists and preferences `ReviewFixAgent` is empty, copy the project fix agent into preferences.\n4. Save clone preferences.\n5. Delete `review` and `review_fix_agent` from the raw project settings map.\n6. Write `.entire/settings.json` back with `jsonutil.MarshalIndentWithNewline`.\n\nThis preserves unrelated project settings and avoids overwriting existing local preferences.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Implement prompt behavior**\n\nAdd a helper shaped roughly like:\n\n```go\nfunc maybePromptReviewSettingsMigration(\n\tctx context.Context,\n\tout io.Writer,\n\terrOut io.Writer,\n\tpromptYN func(context.Context, string, bool) (bool, error),\n) error\n```\n\nBehavior:\n\n- If no project review keys exist: return nil and do not prompt.\n- If non-interactive: print a warning and return nil.\n- If interactive: prompt with default `false`.\n- If accepted: migrate and print a short confirmation.\n- If declined: return nil, leaving project settings unchanged so the prompt appears next time.\n\nUse `interactive.CanPromptInteractively()` plus `interactive.IsTerminalWriter(out)` for production. If this is hard to test, factor the production helper around a smaller testable helper that accepts `canPrompt bool`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Wire migration into command flow**\n\nIn `NewCommand.RunE`, after flag/mode validation and before `--edit`, `--findings`, `--fix`, or normal review handling, call the migration helper:\n\n```go\nif err := maybePromptReviewSettingsMigration(ctx, cmd.OutOrStdout(), cmd.ErrOrStderr(), deps.PromptYN); err != nil {\n\treturn err\n}\n```\n\nIf `deps.PromptYN` is nil, use the existing real y/N prompt implementation. If `realPromptYN` is unexported in `synthesis_sink.go`, keep the migration helper in package `review` so it can call it.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run migration tests and verify pass**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/review -run 'TestReviewSettingsMigration' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: pass.\n\n---\n\n### Task 4: Full Review Package And Settings Verification\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify as needed based on failures:\n  - `cmd/entire/cli/review/cmd_test.go`\n  - `cmd/entire/cli/review/picker_test.go`\n  - `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Run targeted packages**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings ./cmd/entire/cli/review -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: pass.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Fix tests that assume `SaveReviewConfig` writes `.entire/settings.json`**\n\nMany `review/cmd_test.go` tests call `SaveReviewConfig` as setup. After Task 2, those tests should still pass because `settings.Load` reads clone preferences. If any test directly reads `.entire/settings.json`, retarget it to effective `settings.Load` or `settings.LoadClonePreferences`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Run broader unit tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/... -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: pass. If this is too slow locally, at minimum keep `settings` and `review` green and record the broader test limitation before final handoff.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Format and lint**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nmise run fmt\nmise run lint\n```\n\nExpected: pass. If `mise run fmt` changes files, rerun:\n\n```bash\nmise run lint\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Final status check**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngit status --short\n```\n\nExpected: only intentional source/test changes. The ignored spec and plan files under `docs/superpowers` may not appear.\n\n---\n\n## Commit Guidance\n\nUse one or two logical commits, not a commit per TDD step:\n\n1. `fix(review): store review config in clone-local preferences`\n2. Optional split if large: `test(review): cover review config migration`\n\nDo not commit `docs/superpowers/...` unless explicitly asked.\n"}},"status":"completed"}}
